<article class="env-lemma" id="0GIH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GIH">Lemma <span data-tag="0GIH">32.4.21</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits X_ i$ be a directed limit of schemes over $S$ with affine transition morphisms. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$S$ quasi-separated, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X_ i$ quasi-compact and quasi-separated, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the transition morphisms $X_{i'} \to X_ i$ are closed immersions, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X_ i \to S$ locally of finite type, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X \to S$ an immersion. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $X_ i \to S$ is an immersion for $i$ large enough. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose an open subscheme $U \subset S$ such that $X \to S$ factors as a closed immersion $X \to U$ composed with the inclusion morphism $U \to S$. Since $X$ is quasi-compact, we may shrink $U$ and assume $U$ is quasi-compact. Denote $V_ i \subset X_ i$ the inverse image of $U$. Since $V_ i$ pulls back to $X$ we see that $V_ i = X_ i$ for all $i$ large enough by Lemma <a href="/tag/01Z4" data-tag="01Z4">32.4.11</a>. Thus we may assume $X = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits X_ i$ in the category of schemes over $U$. Then we see that $X_ i \to U$ is a closed immersion for $i$ large enough by Lemma <a href="/tag/0A0N" data-tag="0A0N">32.4.20</a>. This proves the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>